Title: Unexpected UART idle interrupt

Body:
I am using the STM32H563VIT6 chip. I am receiving data via UART using DMA, and I have configured the DMA in circular linked-list mode. Below is my code.

However, I have encountered a problem: as soon as I initialize the UART and DMA, a UART idle interrupt is triggered, even though no data has been received — I haven’t sent any data to it at all.

This unexpected idle interrupt interferes with my program’s logic, and I don’t want it to happen. I don’t understand why the idle interrupt is triggered; logically, it shouldn’t be generated if no data has been received.

Please help me. Thank you!

> By the way, my program is written in C++.

cpp
